    "plain": "Extending the soft drinks levy raises modest additional tax revenue and could reduce NHS costs over time, but independent analysts say the health impact is very small, so any long-term fiscal saving is likely limited. The advertising restrictions are regulatory and impose minimal direct cost to the Exchequer.",
